<title>BRAZIL: CVRD, Cemig to build power plant.</title>
<headline>CVRD, Cemig to build power plant.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium including Brazil's Cemig and Companhia Vale do Rio was awarded a contract to build a 110 million reais ($103.5 million) hydroelectric plant in Minas Gerais state, Cemig said.</p>
<p>The group is made up of Cemig and Vale, which each hold a 20 percent stake in the consortium; Coteminas, with 14 percent and Nova Era Silicom, which holds the remaining 46 percent, Cemig said in a statement.</p>
<p>The amount of energy each participant will buy from the new plant will be according to its share in the consortium, it said.</p>
<p>The plant will have an output capacity of 114 megawatts and will be located in Santo Antonio river in the eastern part of Minas Gerais state, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
